payload.text:
To fix this error, you need to run the following SQL in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. 

This script will ensure the `profiles` table exists, add the missing `is_whatsapp` column, and set up the necessary columns for your Admin Dashboard (like `total_spent` and `location`).

```sql
-- 1. Ensure the profiles table exists with all required columns
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.profiles (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users ON DELETE CASCADE,
  full_name text,
  phone text,
  location text,
  is_whatsapp boolean DEFAULT true,
  total_spent numeric DEFAULT 0,
  orders_count integer DEFAULT 0,
  updated_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now()
);

-- 2. Specifically add is_whatsapp if the table existed but missed it
DO $$ 
BEGIN 
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns 
                 WHERE table_name='profiles' AND column_name='is_whatsapp') THEN
    ALTER TABLE public.profiles ADD COLUMN is_whatsapp boolean DEFAULT true;
  END IF;
END $$;

-- 3. Enable Row Level Security
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- 4. Set up Policies so the app can read/write data
-- Allow users to insert/update their own profile during signup
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can insert their own profile" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert their own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can update their own profile" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Users can update their own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);

-- Allow users to see their own profile
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can read their own profile" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Users can read their own profile" ON public.profiles
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = id);

-- Allow service role/admin to see all profiles (needed for your Admin Dashboard)
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Enable read access for all users" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Enable read access for all users" ON public.profiles
  FOR SELECT USING (true);

-- 5. Bonus: Create the orders table (needed for Checkout.tsx)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.orders (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid REFERENCES auth.users,
  items jsonb,
  total_amount numeric,
  delivery_mode text,
  delivery_point text,
  status text DEFAULT 'pending',
  created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now()
);

ALTER TABLE public.orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can insert their own orders" ON public.orders;
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert their own orders" ON public.orders
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can view their own orders" ON public.orders;
CREATE POLICY "Users can view their own orders" ON public.orders
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

### Why this happened:
The "schema cache" error occurs because when you call `supabase.from('profiles').upsert(...)`, the Supabase API looks for the columns in the database. If you added the `is_whatsapp` field in your React code but didn't create that column in the Postgres database, the request fails. Running the SQL above creates the physical column to match your code.

